==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|mis-|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{term|mis-||mis-|lang=ang}}, from Proto-Germanic {{recons|missa-||wrongly, badly|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro}} {{recons|mitto||mutual, reciprocal|lang=ine-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro}} {{recons|meyt-||to replace, switch, exchange, swap|lang=ine-pro}}. Cognate with {{etyl|sco|-}} {{term|mis-||mis-|lang=sco}}, {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|mis-||mis-|lang=nl}}, {{etyl|de|-}} {{term|miss-|lang=de}}, {{term|mis-||mis-|lang=de}}, {{etyl|sv|-}} {{term|mis-||mis-|lang=sv}}, {{etyl|is|-}} {{term|mis-||mis-|lang=is}}. Compare also {{etyl|fr|-}} {{term|més-|lang=fr}}, {{term|mé-||mis-|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|mes-||mis-|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|frk|en}} {{recons|mis-|lang=frk}}, {{recons|missa-||mis-|lang=frk}}, from the same Proto-Germanic source above.

===Prefix===
{{en-prefix}}

# [[bad]], [[badly]], [[wrong]], [[wrongly]]
# [[lack]] or [[failure]]

